  "_about": "Phrases that mark a sentence in a collected document as stating a relationship, so the document collector keeps it as a passage (a doc_passage property on the File) for the statement model to read. A sentence is kept when it names something the document links (a host name, an email address, the author or company) and contains one of these phrases, or when it names two such things. phrase is matched without case on word boundaries. kinds are the statement kinds the phrase suggests; each kind names the inference families that may consume such statements, and a phrase may suggest several. basis cites the vocabulary term the kind follows (the W3C Organization Ontology, schema.org). Passages are observations of what a document says; nothing here concludes a relationship. Add phrases here, not in Go code.",
  "max_passages": 20,
  "max_passage_chars": 400,
  "kinds": {
    "org_structure": {"families": ["ownership", "org_unit", "family"], "basis": "https://www.w3.org/TR/vocab-org/#org:subOrganizationOf"},
    "role": {"families": ["people", "identity"], "basis": "https://www.w3.org/TR/vocab-org/#org:Post"},
    "membership": {"families": ["people", "affiliation"], "basis": "https://www.w3.org/TR/vocab-org/#org:memberOf"},
    "funding": {"families": ["funding", "affiliation"], "basis": "https://schema.org/funder"},
    "partnership": {"families": ["affiliation"], "basis": "https://schema.org/member"},
    "supplier": {"families": ["vendors", "services"], "basis": "https://schema.org/provider"},
    "product_use": {"families": ["services", "vulnerable_software"], "basis": "https://schema.org/instrument"},
    "change": {"families": ["identity", "duplicates", "family"], "basis": "https://www.w3.org/TR/vocab-org/#org:ChangeEvent"},
    "location": {"families": ["geography", "contacts"], "basis": "https://schema.org/location"}
  },
  "cues": [
    {"phrase": "a division of", "kinds": ["org_structure"]},
    {"phrase": "a department of", "kinds": ["org_structure"]},
    {"phrase": "a unit of", "kinds": ["org_structure"]},
